<title>SWITZERLAND: Nestle plans no share buy-back.</title>
<headline>Nestle plans no share buy-back.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nestle SA said a share buy-back, currently a popular move among Swiss companies, is not being considered at the time being.</p>
<p>&quot;If Swiss tax rules are changed, we will review this, But it is not an issue at this time,&quot; Nestle chief financial officer Mario Corti told a news conference.</p>
<p>He said the nominal value of Nestle's shares was already at the Swiss legal minimum of 10 francs and the company wants a strong capital base to finance internal growth.</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
</text>
